--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. peeksafe has zero runtime dependencies, vendors no source, and ships no
code it did not write. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` asserts the first of those on
every pull request by packing the tarball, installing it into an empty project,
and failing if `npm ls` resolves more than two packages.

Development dependencies (TypeScript, vitest, @types/node) are not redistributed
and are not part of the published package.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Algorithms and published constants
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything statistical here is implemented from published closed forms and
recurrences rather than ported from an existing implementation. Mathematical
methods and tabulated constants are not anybody's intellectual property, but
naming their sources is both good manners and the fastest way for a reader to
check the arithmetic.

  Regularized incomplete beta       Continued fraction: Abramowitz & Stegun,
  src/stats.ts                      Handbook of Mathematical Functions, 26.5.8.
                                    Evaluated by the modified Lentz algorithm:
                                    Lentz (1976), amended by Thompson & Barnett
                                    (1986).

  log Γ(x)                          Lanczos approximation, g = 7, n = 9. The
  src/stats.ts                      coefficient set is the widely reprinted one
                                    originating with Lanczos (1964).

  Φ⁻¹(p)                            Peter Acklam's algorithm for the inverse
  src/stats.ts                      normal CDF, refined here by one Halley
                                    step. Acklam released it for unrestricted
                                    use.

  Lower incomplete gamma            Standard series and continued-fraction
  src/stats.ts                      expansions, Abramowitz & Stegun 6.5.

  Linear congruential generator     Multiplier 1664525, increment 1013904223,
  src/rand.ts                       modulus 2^32. Tabulated parameters from
                                    Knuth, The Art of Computer Programming,
                                    volume 2.

  32-bit avalanche (mix32)          The `lowbias32` multipliers from Chris
  src/rand.ts                       Wellons' hash function prospector, placed
                                    by the author in the public domain.

  hash32                            FNV-1a. Public domain by the authors'
  src/rand.ts                       explicit statement.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Statistical methods
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The procedures peeksafe implements are established results. README.md is
explicit about which of this library's claims are new and which are not, and
RESEARCH-NOTES.md records an adversarial literature check that withdrew two of
four originally-claimed novelties.

  e-values and testing by betting   Shafer; Grünwald, de Heide & Koolen (Safe
                                    Testing); Waudby-Smith & Ramdas.
  e-BH                              Wang & Ramdas, False discovery rate control
                                    with e-values (2022).
  Stopped e-BH                      Wang, Dandapanthula & Ramdas (2025).
  Benjamini-Hochberg                Benjamini & Hochberg (1995).
  Sequential probability ratio      Wald, Sequential Analysis (1945).
  McNemar's test                    McNemar (1947).
  Cluster-robust variance (CR2)     Liang & Zeger (1986); Bell & McCaffrey
                                    (2002).
  Bayes factor asymptotics          Kass & Raftery (1995).
  Spectrum bias                     Ransohoff & Feinstein (1978).
